-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Discord bridge (bridge/)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The bridge is a separate Python program that dollcore starts as a child process
when [bridge] is enabled; none of it is compiled into dollcore. Its dependencies
are installed by uv from bridge/uv.lock into bridge/.venv. Licenses as declared
in the installed packages' metadata:

- py-cord (pinned to a git commit), MIT
- davey 0.1.7, MIT
- numpy, BSD-3-Clause (with bundled parts under 0BSD, MIT, Zlib, CC0-1.0)
- aiohttp, Apache-2.0 AND MIT; aiohappyeyeballs, PSF-2.0; aiosignal, frozenlist,
  multidict, propcache, yarl, Apache-2.0; attrs, MIT; idna, BSD-3-Clause;
  pynacl, Apache-2.0; cffi, MIT-0; pycparser, BSD-3-Clause;
  typing-extensions, PSF-2.0
- test only: pytest, iniconfig, pluggy, MIT; pytest-asyncio, Apache-2.0;
  packaging, Apache-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause; pygments, BSD-2-Clause
- colorama is in the lock file for Windows only and is not installed on macOS.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Models
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No model weights are part of this repository. dollcore downloads the memory
embedding model (Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B) and, with [voice] enabled, the
Qwen3-TTS bundles named in the config from Hugging Face at first use; they
remain under their own licenses. The language model is the person's own server.
